{"exchanges":[{"user":"How do collagen and elastin contribute to the skin’s strength and flexibility?","assistant":"Collagen and elastin are key structural proteins found primarily in the middle skin layer, and they play fundamental roles in maintaining the skin's strength and flexibility. Collagen forms a dense network of fibers that provides tensile strength, essentially acting as the skin’s scaffolding. This network prevents the skin from tearing or stretching excessively, giving it a firm, supportive framework that helps maintain its shape and resilience.

